          "handle": "AustinJustice",
          "creator": "@AustinJustice",
          "text": "An Atlanta woman told her mother, \"Mommy, he's going to kill me.\" She'd already gotten a restraining order on her crazy ex. He kept harassing her anyway -- broke into her home, smashed all her windows. Then one afternoon he confronted her at the end of her street and shot her multiple times inside her SUV. She crashed trying to get away and died at the scene. Police activated Flock cameras to tag his plate and got him arrested within hours before he could become a fugitive and hurt more people. Merinda Henderson was 44.",
          "link": "https://nitter.net/AustinJustice/status/2080725486993293786#m",
