        {
          "handle": "AustinJustice",
          "creator": "@AustinJustice",
          "text": "Austin had the largest homicide increase of any big city in the country even as murder fell almost everywhere else. Nationally, murders are down 18% in a year and 31% since 2019, heading toward the lowest rate since 1900! Murder rate 2019-2026: - Baltimore down 68% - Washington DC down 43% - St. Louis down 41% - Detroit down 34% Austin's homicide rate is up 74%.",
